<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Heading and Paragraph Activity</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>This is a Main Heading (H1)</h1>
    <p>This is a paragraph. Paragraphs are used to write regular text on a webpage. The H1 tag is usually used for the main title.</p>

    <h2>This is a Subheading (H2)</h2>
    <p>This is another paragraph under the H2 heading. Headings help organize your content into sections.</p>
    
    <h3>This is a Smaller Heading (H3)</h3>
    <p>You can use tags all the way down to H6 for smaller, less important headings. Notice how the text size gets smaller with each heading level!</p>

</body>
</html>
